WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:05.310
It's really been an interesting four years
from Sean Hannity, he went from already prominent

00:00:05.310 --> 00:00:11.130
right wing propagandist on Fox News, really
to a presidential insider, I mean, a friend

00:00:11.130 --> 00:00:17.390
of Donald Trump's who not so much recently,
but certainly earlier on in his administration,

00:00:17.390 --> 00:00:20.300
Hannity and Trump often speaking on the phone
at night.

00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:24.830
Hannity was sometimes the last person Trump
would speak to before, I guess, going to bed.

00:00:24.830 --> 00:00:26.830
If that's something Donald Trump does, I don't
know.

00:00:26.830 --> 00:00:30.180
He doesn't really seem to do anything the
way most of us do.

00:00:30.180 --> 00:00:35.690
But in any case, Sean Hannity had really become
an insider, sometimes traveling on Trump's

00:00:35.690 --> 00:00:37.600
helicopter or on Air Force One.

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:41.400
He would do these sycophantic softball interviews
of Trump.

00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:45.829
He would do sycophantic interviews of Kayleigh
McEnany and many others.

00:00:45.829 --> 00:00:50.690
Well, Sean Hannity's ratings have absolutely
collapsed since the election.

00:00:50.690 --> 00:00:54.100
And Eric Boehlert has some great reporting
on this.

00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:59.449
Fox has actually been touting the latest ratings
numbers as a big win for Sean Hannity.

00:00:59.449 --> 00:01:01.520
And a lot of publications fell for it.

00:01:01.520 --> 00:01:05.680
And they put together headlines that make
it seem like everything is going great for

00:01:05.680 --> 00:01:06.680
Hannity.

00:01:06.680 --> 00:01:11.009
Fox, for example, running an article on December
16th called Sean Hannity.

00:01:11.009 --> 00:01:19.149
Tucker Carlson set records as Fox News makes
history in 20/20 cable news ratings.

00:01:19.149 --> 00:01:23.689
But the truth is there has been a massive
decline.

00:01:23.689 --> 00:01:29.579
Hannity's show falling into last place for
the nine p.m. time slot among what's called

00:01:29.579 --> 00:01:34.810
the key demographic, the 25 to 54 demographic.

00:01:34.810 --> 00:01:39.319
Hannity stuck in that last place for two months
now.

00:01:39.319 --> 00:01:45.609
Now, it is true that Hannity still has a ton
of viewers in the aggregate, but the declines

00:01:45.609 --> 00:01:46.719
have been significant.

00:01:46.719 --> 00:01:54.209
And part of the reason is people are abandoning
Fox for further loony right wing content on

00:01:54.209 --> 00:01:56.279
Newsmax and on.

00:01:56.279 --> 00:02:00.999
And I've been teasing that later this week,
we're going to look in detail at an incredible

00:02:00.999 --> 00:02:04.909
a focus group done by Frank Luntz with Trump
hosts.

00:02:04.909 --> 00:02:08.310
And many of them say Fox is too left.

00:02:08.310 --> 00:02:09.569
We're now with Newsmax.

00:02:09.569 --> 00:02:15.920
And and so part of Hannity's decline is that
and they're sort of good and bad.

00:02:15.920 --> 00:02:21.140
They're it's good that fewer people are watching
Hannity, but it's bad that lots of them are

00:02:21.140 --> 00:02:23.549
watching something even crazier.

00:02:23.549 --> 00:02:30.650
Instead, others have abandoned Hannity and
they started to in December when it became

00:02:30.650 --> 00:02:39.150
clear that all of Hannity's commentary about
